/github.com/amarsero","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amarsero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amarsero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amarsero/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amarsero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amarsero/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amarsero/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amarsero/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amarsero/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amarsero/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The problem is that `EditorData::script_class_save_icon_paths` has access to the icon paths for all scripts, while `ScriptServer::save_global_classes` has all the other properties but only for global scripts.\r\nA quick fix is to make `ScriptServer` a friend of `EditorData`, and keep only `ScriptServer::save_global_classes`. \r\nA more complete solution would be to use `ScriptServer::get_class_icon_path` as the source of truth for global script icons while using`EditorData::_script_class_icon_paths` for the others. But this would make the code more confusing.\r\n","created_at":"2025-02-12T16:50:41Z","updated_at":"2025-02-12T16:50:41Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102636#discussion_r1953049400","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/102636","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1953049400"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102636#discussion_r1953049400"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/102636"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1953049400/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0